.TH RUNNER 1 "2026-08-18" "runner 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
runner \- TUI project script runner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runner
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B runner
is an interactive terminal (TUI) launcher for per-project commands. It reads a
.B runner.toml
file describing a set of actions, presents them in a selectable list, and runs
the chosen action in a child shell while streaming its output \(em including
256-color and truecolor ANSI \(em into a scrolling pane.
.PP
With no options,
.B runner
searches upward from the current directory for
.B runner.toml
and opens the interactive UI. Exactly one action runs at a time; an action's
working directory is resolved relative to the config file.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR \(ua / \(da ", " k / j
Select the previous/next action.
.TP
.B Enter
Run the selected action.
.TP
.BR PgUp / PgDn ", " End ", mouse wheel"
Scroll the output pane.
.TP
.B mouse drag
Select text in the output pane.
.TP
.B y
Copy the current selection to the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Y
Copy the full output of the last command to the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Kill the running child process.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Quit.
.PP
Clipboard copy uses an OSC 52 terminal escape (works over SSH/tmux) and, when
available, an external tool
.RB ( wl\-copy ", " xclip / xsel ", or " pbcopy ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Use \fIPATH\fR as the config file instead of searching for
.BR runner.toml .
.TP
.B \-\-generate\-config
Write a starter
.B runner.toml
into the current directory. Refuses to overwrite an existing file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Actions are declared as an array of tables. Each
.B [[action]]
supports:
.TP
.B label
Short name shown in the list (required).
.TP
.B cmd
Command run via \fB/bin/sh -c\fR (required).
.TP
.B desc
One-line description (optional).
.TP
.B group
Group heading the action is listed under (optional).
.TP
.B cwd
Working directory, resolved relative to the config file (optional).
.TP
.B env
Table of environment variables set for the action's child process (optional).
.PP
The string fields
.B cwd
and each
.B env
value support
.BI ${ VAR }
expansion against
.BR runner 's
own environment, resolved when the config is loaded. An undefined variable is a
load error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ./runner.toml
Per-project action definitions (searched for upward from the current directory).
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/doc/runner/runner.toml.example
Installed example configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Config not found, config error, or a runtime failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.SH AUTHOR
Ethan Saenger
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/removingnest109/runner
